From a0618837804ba3795cfd2f01be466f8019d3c356 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Glim Data <glimdata@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 16:55:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] protocols: Copy the pids block when it is present, not
 when it is absent

The grpc-to-OCI conversion of LinuxResources copied Pids under the
inverted condition, so a limit sent by the runtime was dropped and an
absent one became a LinuxPids with limit 0. Use the same positive check
as the other resource blocks, and add a round-trip test.

