From c02a55b3d06851b9e496f4cff637d99c6af9c81a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Glim Data <glimdata@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 16:55:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] runtime-rs: Keep the OCI pids limit in the spec sent to
 the guest

The container create path cleared linux.resources.pids together with
devices, block I/O and network before the spec reached the agent, so
pids.max was never applied in the guest and a fork storm was bounded
only by the VM size. The agent's cgroup manager applies the limit when
the block is present, so keep it, and move the clearing of the other
blocks into a function with a test.

Fixes: #13824

